data_tite2
# Phase identity: ambient 1T-TiTe2, P-3m1, one formula unit per cell.
# Provenance: experimental geometry from Kuznetsova et al., Phys. Rev. B 72,
# 085418 (2005), cross-checked against NIST JARVIS JVASP-335. The P1 basis is
# encoded independently from the public JARVIS record using experimental a,c,z.
# The Te-Ti-Te sheets stack along c, giving cleavage surface (001).
# Limiting checks: V=(sqrt(3)/2)a^2c, 1Ti+2Te, finite basal (001) coupling.
# Validation: tite2-p3m1-structure
_symmetry_space_group_name_H-M 'P 1'
_symmetry_Int_Tables_number 1
_cell_length_a 3.777
_cell_length_b 3.777
_cell_length_c 6.498
_cell_angle_alpha 90.0
_cell_angle_beta 90.0
_cell_angle_gamma 120.0
